    "title": "Super 25 national champion Buford to take on Baylor in preseason clash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joseph Spears ,\n8 hours ago\nArguably one of the biggest matchups for the 2026 high school football season has been announced and it's a showdown that won't count on either teams record.\nThat Baylor School (Chattanooga, TN) announced on X Wednesday afternoon a scheduled preseason scrimmage against Buford (GA). The teams are set to meet at Philip Beard Stadium on August 7 at 7:30 p.m. ET.\nBoth teams finished the 2025 season unbeaten and ranked as top 15 teams in the final 2025 USA TODAY Sports Super 25 rankings.\nBuford finished as the No. 1 team in the nation while Baylor came in at No. 13.\nThe Wolves dominated Georgia's high school football season in 2025 going 15-0, beating teams by an average of 33.6 points and beating Carrollton 28-21 for the GHSA Class 6A state championship.\nFor Baylor, the Red Raiders finished the 2025 season with a 12-0 record. They won the TSSAA Division II-AAA championship with a 28-24 win over Brentwood Academy.\nWhile Buford will be looking to replace several key figures from last year's championship team, Baylor is led by five-star running back and two-time defending Division II-AAA Mr. Football David Gabriel Georges. Baylor also added four-star Ole Miss quarterback pledge and Elite 11 finalist Keegan Croucher in the offseason.\nBuford is scheduled to kick off its season against on ESPN on August 22 against Gainesville (GA) . Baylor starts its season two days earlier at home in a rematch of the 2025 Division II-AAA championship against Brentwood Academy.\nThis article originally appeared on USA TODAY: Super 25 national champion Buford to take on Baylor in preseason clash",
    "summary": "Arguably one of the biggest matchups for the 2026 high school football season has been announced and it's a showdown that won't count on either teams record. That Baylor School (Chattanooga, TN) announced on X Wednesday afternoon a scheduled preseason scrimmage against Buford (GA). While Buford will be looking to replace several key figures from last year's championship team, Baylor is led by five-star running back and two-time defending Division II-AAA Mr. Football David Gabriel Georges. Baylor also added four-star Ole Miss quarterback pledge and Elite 11 finalist Keegan Croucher in the offseason.",
